    <statement><p>Match each polar equation below to the best description.
Possible answers are C,E,H,L,P,R,S,V,and Z.</p>
<p><em> C. </em> Circle centered at origin</p>
<p><em> E. </em> Ellipse</p>
<p><em> H. </em> Hyperbola</p>
<p><em> L. </em> Line neither vertical nor horizontal</p>
<p><em> P. </em> Parabola</p>
<p><em> R. </em> Circle not centered at origin</p>
<p><em> S. </em> Spiral</p>
<p><em> V. </em> Vertical Line</p>
<p><em> Z. </em> Horizontal Line</p>
<p>POLAR EQUATIONS</p>
</statement>
